From 8cde8997813389915133ab5932c04085a9fcc7d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(gateway): authenticate API keys bound to tenants

The gateway "authenticated" a request when it carried any X-Tenant-ID
value, so a caller could act as any tenant by choosing the header. The
unused AuthzWithToken checked a static token list that was not bound to
a tenant at all.

Add an Authenticator interface with two implementations:

* APIKeyAuthenticator (GATEWAY_AUTH_MODE=apikey, the default): resolves
  "Authorization: Bearer <key>" through GATEWAY_API_KEYS_FILE, the same
  SHA-256-only key file format the control plane reads. A tenant header
  that disagrees with the key's tenant is rejected with 403.
* HeaderAuthenticator (GATEWAY_AUTH_MODE=dev): the previous header trust,
  only accepted when the gateway listens on a loopback address.

The Authenticate middleware stores the principal in the request context
and overwrites the tenant header with the verified tenant. Failures use
the control plane's error envelope; 401s carry WWW-Authenticate. The
bearer scheme is matched case-insensitively (RFC 7235).

Inference calls require the read scope. The resolver forwards the
caller's Authorization header so the control plane can verify the caller
itself, and a 403 from the control plane surfaces as 403 instead of 502.
Startup fails when the mode is unknown or the key file is missing or
invalid. "make run-dev" starts a local dev-mode gateway.
